Upstream-Status: Inappropriate

Subject: [PATCH] mm/vmstat: Don't dirty idle per-cpu NUMA counters when folding

fold_vm_zone_numa_events() does an xchg() on every NUMA event counter of
every online CPU and zone, each time /proc/vmstat or a node's numastat is
read.  CPUs that did not allocate since the last fold get their
cachelines written for nothing.

Only xchg() counters that are not zero.
---
--- a/mm/vmstat.c
+++ b/mm/vmstat.c
@@ -179,8 +179,11 @@ static void fold_vm_zone_numa_events(struct zone *zone)
 		struct per_cpu_zonestat *pzstats;
 
 		pzstats = per_cpu_ptr(zone->per_cpu_zonestats, cpu);
-		for (item = 0; item < NR_VM_NUMA_EVENT_ITEMS; item++)
+		for (item = 0; item < NR_VM_NUMA_EVENT_ITEMS; item++) {
+			if (!READ_ONCE(pzstats->vm_numa_event[item]))
+				continue;
 			zone_numa_events[item] += xchg(&pzstats->vm_numa_event[item], 0);
+		}
 	}
 
 	for (item = 0; item < NR_VM_NUMA_EVENT_ITEMS; item++)
